  "discussion": "A small, medium-period northwest swell will provide a small boost to surf along north-facing shores as it peaks today. The swell fades tonight into Saturday as a new moderate, medium-period north- northwest swell arrives and builds on Saturday. Surf along north and west-facing shores will quickly increase through the day and peak around seasonal average on Sunday. As this swell declines on Monday, a long-period west-northwest swell will arrive, maintaining small to moderate surf into the middle of next week. Small background level surf will prevail along south-facing shores today. A small, medium-period south-southwest swell will bring a small bump to surf tonight into Saturday, with small to moderate, long- period energy filling in on Sunday. This will push surf back to around seasonal average into early next week. Along east-facing shores, trade-wind swell will continue to decrease. However, a small, medium-period northeast swell may maintain small surf through Saturday. Aside from wrapping north- northwest swell in exposed areas, east shore surf should remain below seasonal average much of next week.",
